## 5. A candidate ambient-complex model `[CANDIDATE-NEW]`

The requirement: each enterprise enforces gluing only over its own admitted territory; the ambient market can retain disagreement. This is **not** what Wd/ùìó as defined does ‚Äî Wd/ùìó is defined so that only *settled* (stabilized, Boolean) content survives entry, and its terminal/colimit status means the whole construction is oriented toward a single coherent recipient. A market that must retain disagreement cannot be built by relabeling that object; it needs different coefficients and no forced global gluing.

**Sketch**, built mostly from pieces already proved or specified elsewhere in the archive:

- Let **N** be the *nerve* of declared treaty relations: vertices are sovereign settlements `E_i`; higher simplices exist only where settlements have declared border contracts, exactly Source 7 ¬ß2's "territory presented as local records over a cover."
- Each `E_i` is its own site `(T_i, J_i)` and genuinely **is** a Grothendieck topos `Sh(T_i, J_i)` with its own enforced sheaf condition ‚Äî sections over any cover of `T_i` glue uniquely *inside* `E_i`. This is the intra-enterprise gluing AGENTS.md requires ("An enterprise is the region over which gluing is enforced"), and it maps naturally onto A2A as the internal coordination face.
- A claim-state presheaf **C** lives over **N**, valued not in Boolean `H*` but in **FOUR** or the Record monoid (Source 9 ¬ß1, ¬ß12j(c)) ‚Äî a coefficient system able to hold "for," "against," "both," and "neither" without exploding or flattening.
- Restriction maps `C(E_i) ‚Üí C(B_ij)` at a border `B_ij` are **settlement-controlled projections**, each `E_i` deciding under its own law what it discloses to a given counterparty ‚Äî not a single universal `Stab`.
- **N** together with **C** is only ever required to be a *presheaf*, never a sheaf. A "global section of the market" ‚Äî one univocal, mesh-wide settled state ‚Äî is **not asserted to exist**. Its absence is *measured*, not repaired: the cycle rank of **N**'s incidence pattern (`[THEOREM]`, Source 7 ¬ß2) is a computable lower bound on unavoidable disagreement, and disagreement across three or more pairwise-fine settlements is exactly the kind of nonzero Massey/H¬π-type class already machine-checked to exist for FOUR/Record coefficients on comparable covers (`hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy`, Source 9 ¬ß5, ¬ß12j).
- Root, if it appears in this diagram at all, is a **witness of the nerve** ‚Äî it may observe which border contracts exist ‚Äî never a colimit vertex, never an authority to write any `E_i`'s pools.

This model is explicitly **not** Wd/ùìó: no colimit is forced, coefficients are contradiction-carrying rather than Boolean-settled, and gluing is scoped strictly to each settlement's own territory. It reuses Source 7's obstruction apparatus and Source 9's proved gluing-failure results, applied to a settlement-shaped cover rather than the dyadic cylinder cover they were originally proved on ‚Äî an extension, not a citation.

---

## 6. Pools as borders, never as unowned write portals

The archived pool (`Phase_U ‚Ü™ U`, Source 1/2) is a genuine, established `[THEOREM]`-grade object, but it has a structural gap relative to what a border requires. As written:

- The **yellow ring** (egress) is universal and requires no destination check ‚Äî fine for a *publication* act, but as specified it also *strips* unsettled content (`H \ H*` "does not survive the transition"). A border that only ever exposes stripped, settled-only content cannot carry the contested claims a treaty seam needs to arbitrate.
- The **green ring** (ingress) is described as an unconditional injective map ‚Äî "you must choose a pool... before you can enter" concerns *which* world, never *whether* that world admits you. There is no admission predicate anywhere in Sources 1‚Äì3's portal machinery.

Read literally, a "pool" instantiated this way is exactly the "unowned write portal" AGENTS.md forbids: any counterparty holding the right ring could inject settled content into a world's fiber without that world's law having any say. This is not a small omission ‚Äî it is the single most direct collision between the archived math and adopted settlement law.

**Consequence for the interpretation:** pools may be *read* as borders, treaty seams, or admission surfaces only if augmented with (1) a receiving-settlement-controlled admission predicate before any cross-territory write, and (2) a receipt (x402-shaped) recording the crossing. Neither augmentation exists in the archive. Adopting "pool = border" without adding both is a nonclaim (¬ß10).

---

## 7. Old modal-collapse picture vs. adopted market: a direct comparison

| Axis | Archived Wood/hyperverse `[CONJECTURE/ARCHIVED-PROPOSAL]` | Adopted settlement law `[ADOPTED]` |
|---|---|---|
| Endgame | Modal Collapse is explicitly the *win condition*: "stop writing to the world and watch it settle" (Source 3) | No endgame; legitimacy is "least settlement" of *currently* witnessed evidence, continuously re-derivable, with drift tracked as a live quantity (Source 7 ¬ß7) |
| Value carrier | Boolean `H*` after collapse; Heyting pre-collapse but stripped on entry to ùìó | FOUR / Record ‚Äî chosen precisely because Boolean carriers "can only explode or flatten" under contradiction (Source 7 ¬ß4) |
| Disagreement | Transient by design; everything not yet settled is headed toward erasure via `Stab` | Borders are *permanently* certified when discharge would collapse protected content ‚Äî not transitional, not scheduled for resolution |
| Provenance | Explicitly forgotten ("animals forget their world of origin," presentation independence) | Mandatory: EAVT/Datom monotone source log, x402 receipts, attributed claims |
| Topology of the mesh | One central recipient (Wd/ùìó) mediating a finite family `{W_i}` | Polycentric mesh, no capital, no universal work pool, no single recipient object (Source 5 ¬ß7) |

The corpus itself states the incompatibility sharply and in its own voice, without needing this report to invent the tension: **"Convergence guarantees and the capacity for sovereignty exclude each other at the type level"** (Source 7 ¬ß4). Modal Collapse is a convergence guarantee. Sovereignty, as adopted, requires the capacity it excludes. A literal Wood-as-market therefore cannot be adopted as stated; it can at most donate vocabulary to a differently-typed construction (¬ß5).

---

## 8. Presentation independence vs. node-local books and accountability

Source 1 states plainly that ùìó* "forgets the initial alphabet Œ£ and independence relation I" and that a traveller "sheds trace-specific provenance ‚Äî the record of which world produced it is erased at the hyperversal level."

This is flatly incompatible with:

- **Node-local books and causal provenance** (AGENTS.md: `data/` is write-once/append-only; EAVT/Datom is the monotone source log).
- **Receipts and contracts** ‚Äî x402 settles priced boundary crossings; a receipt with no recoverable origin settles nothing.
- **The honesty trichotomy** (Source 7 ¬ß1): every record must be witnessed, derived, or purchased-with-erasure-on-the-books. Origin-forgetting produces the fourth, forbidden class ‚Äî asserted and unpriced.
- **The gauge principle** (Source 7 ¬ß5): a claim acquires evidential standing only by surviving comparisons someone *other than its producer* can re-run; if origin is erased, no such comparison is possible, and the claim reduces to "gauge ‚Äî no evidence, precisely."
- **Accountable attention and correction bonds** (Sources 6, 8): the sellable object is an *attributed, time-indexed* claim with support and correction state; an unattributed claim cannot be corrected, bonded, or trusted.

There is a narrower, legitimate cousin worth distinguishing: **gauge invariance** (Source 7 ¬ß5) says a single reporter's *presentation* of a record may vary freely without loss, so long as its validity on its own patch is preserved. This is about interchangeable *presentations of the same attributed record* ‚Äî it is the opposite operation from origin-forgetting, which erases *which record it was*. The two must not be conflated. Presentation independence, as the Wood defines it, is disqualified for the market reading; gauge invariance, as adopted law defines it, is not affected by this finding and remains available.

---

## 9. Does the market reading need new construction, or is renaming Wd enough?

Renaming is insufficient, for a reason that is structural rather than terminological: **Wd/ùìó's entire construction is oriented around a lossy projection (`Stab`) that discards exactly the content ‚Äî unsettled, contested, `H \ H*` ‚Äî that a market retaining disagreement must keep.** The pool only ever receives what has already been stripped to settled Boolean form. Even setting aside Modal Collapse and Finality as conjectural, the *established* `[THEOREM]`-grade part of the correspondence (stabilization, pool, boundary-determined portal) is architected as a settlement-content-only channel. There is no coefficient slot in the archived construction for "both support and refutation, both standing." Renaming Wd "the market" would misdescribe it: it would still, by its own proved boundary-factorization theorem, refuse to carry a border.

The candidate in ¬ß5 is offered as the minimum departure that satisfies the demand: same *vocabulary* (pools, borders, egress/ingress asymmetry), different *coefficients and gluing scope* (FOUR/Record instead of Boolean; local-only gluing instead of a forced global colimit). That departure is required, not optional.

---

## 10. Relation to settlement membranes, ActivityPub, A2A, MetroPlat, the distal bypass

- **Settlement membranes** (Source 4): each `E_i` in ¬ß5's nerve *is* a membrane ‚Äî the correspondence is direct and unproblematic.
- **A2A** (intra-enterprise): maps onto each settlement's own internal site `(T_i, J_i)` and its internally-enforced gluing ‚Äî the "internal flow" `Flow(W)` of Source 2, kept strictly inside one settlement.
- **ActivityPub** (inter-enterprise): maps onto border-crossing messages between settlements in **N** ‚Äî but only if reinterpreted as consent-gated treaty traffic, not as a universal `Stab`-style broadcast. AGENTS.md already states this allocation; nothing here changes it.
- **MetroPlat**: at most one vertex in the nerve ‚Äî a separately hireable settlement other enterprises may contract with. It is explicitly **not** a candidate for the colimit-recipient role Wd/ùìó conjecturally occupies, and this report makes no claim otherwise. Any future implementation that routes all border traffic through MetroPlat by default would reproduce exactly the "root is not capital" violation the corpus repeatedly warns against (Source 5 ¬ß7).
- **Root/dispatcher**: at most a witness of which border contracts exist (¬ß5) ‚Äî never an enterprise, never a write authority, never the market itself.
- **The distal bypass** (Source 10, itself `[ARCHIVED-PROPOSAL]`, "binds nobody"): its five-step recipe (derive the obstruction sheet ‚Üí classify damage vs. border ‚Üí discharge damage ‚Üí certify borders ‚Üí price every erasure ‚Üí emit certificates) is a **better existing fit** for "the market retaining disagreement" than anything in Sources 1‚Äì3, and ¬ß5's candidate model is essentially this recipe applied to a settlement nerve. Citing it here is not an adoption ‚Äî its own status line is preserved.

---

## 11. Nonclaims

- This report does **not** claim Wd/ùìó = market is adopted architecture. It is tested and found to require modification.
- Does **not** claim Modal Collapse, Finality, or Acyclicity are proved. All remain `[CONJECTURE]`, one of them (Finality/Acyclicity) internally contested by the archive's own Topos-of-Topoi note.
- Does **not** claim the ¬ß5 candidate model exists as a formal construction with proved limits/colimits ‚Äî it is a sketch recombining archived, separately-proved pieces on a new cover, not itself a theorem.
- Does **not** claim MetroPlat, root, or any single enterprise should be, or resembles, the market's terminal recipient.
- Does **not** claim presentation independence or origin-forgetting is adopted anywhere in current law; it is explicitly rejected in ¬ß9.
- Does **not** claim the "Terminal, Not Initial" remark resolves whether a universal mediator *exists* ‚Äî only that it resolves *which direction the arrows point*.
- Does **not** quote or invent Lewis primary text beyond the paraphrases already present in Sources 1‚Äì3.

## 12. Failure cases

- Implementing the market as a literal topos with a mesh-wide sheaf condition silently forces settlement of protected borders, since Boolean `H*` structurally cannot represent "both" ‚Äî this reproduces exactly the type-level exclusion Source 7 ¬ß4 names.
- Implementing pools as the archived green ring (unconditional injective map, no admission predicate) is literally the unowned write portal AGENTS.md forbids.
- Stripping provenance at any stage (literal presentation independence) makes receipts, correction bonds, and EAVT logs unattributable, breaking the honesty trichotomy of Source 7 ¬ß1.

## 13. Falsifiers

- If a FOUR/Record-coefficient presheaf on a settlement-shaped nerve is shown to glue *regardless* of coefficient choice (i.e., `hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy`'s dichotomy fails to extend from the dyadic hull to a settlement nerve), the market-retains-disagreement reading collapses back toward modal collapse and the interpretation fails.
- If, conversely, Source 7 ¬ß3's open "Actuality" conjecture (generic occupancy of the obstruction capacity) is shown to hold for a settlement-shaped nerve, that positively supports the market-as-non-gluing-complex reading.
- If any settlement is found to require importing another settlement's non-admitted data to function, the "borders not portals" reading fails operationally regardless of its formal status.

## 14. Executable engineering consequences

- Do not reuse `Stab` (lossy Boolean projection) as the core operation of any market-facing "publish outward" component; use an obstruction-sheet/certificate emitter (Source 10's recipe) instead.
- Every pool/border implementation must carry a receiving-settlement-controlled admission predicate and emit a receipt on crossing; a bare injective map is disqualified.
- Egress objects must carry full provenance by default; a settled-only summary view is permitted only as an optional projection *alongside* the full record, never as its replacement.
- No component should treat "all disagreement settled" as a completion or success state for the enterprise mesh.

---

## 15. Bounded recommendation

**Usable now, as vocabulary only:** pool ‚Üí border/admission-surface; the two-ring egress/ingress asymmetry as a structural analogy for "publish outward is uniform, admit inward is bespoke per treaty" (once patched with consent-gating, ¬ß7); "obstruction sheet," "damage vs. border," from the distal bypass, which already largely matches AGENTS.md's own "market... sections may disagree" language.

**Held for the Leader, unresolved:** whether to formalize the market as the ¬ß5 candidate (per-settlement sites, FOUR/Record coefficients, no forced mesh-wide gluing) or some other construction; whether "Wood"/"hyperverse" vocabulary should be retired from enterprise use entirely and reserved strictly for the Obsmetrologia/pyfars mathematical and game contexts it was built for; whether pursuing proofs of Modal Collapse/Finality/Acyclicity is worth continued effort given they point structurally away from sovereignty-preserving design.

**Smallest discriminating experiment:** build a minimal three-settlement nerve (a triangle ‚Äî the shape already used for the Massey/Borromean/GHZ example in Source 9 ¬ß12j(e)) with FOUR-valued claim-states at each border, using the already-proved `hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy` and `record_merge_ground_state` machinery applied to this new cover instead of the dyadic cylinder cover it was proved on. If a global Boolean gluing is forced regardless of coefficients, the market-as-Wood reading is falsified. If a genuine, non-erasable obstruction persists and can be certified rather than resolved, the candidate in ¬ß5 is supported and the Wood/hyperverse apparatus is confirmed unsuitable as-is. This experiment is cheap, already mostly built, and decisive.ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GJRsrlSU015y7zWyShocemKzKadMBOLAOEw7zdLvk48ÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx9ni:///sha-256;5XBjgxHe8TTMN_2QzXl1ak3XUuYUvanAxDVK14cl3IkÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WnODHa_U3OQjpcuelOd-sCGugFhYa4PXdIF2S5zctu8ÉdpairÉdleftÅdstarÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÅdunitÇdmark`ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7OM1OYTfjIxiZ-t_DBY2zqEoBUQjmccL-nbtDOw668sÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eL_OC7nDO22CW0AkX9rikCHbWn-JV5AIlLlH0Cq6ouYÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÅdunitÇdmarka1ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jhe96qk1x-2Ipl3C9anI59jpsmVSuhezcKrox9AR78kÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÉcsumÅdunitÅdunitÇdmarkf296.62ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2B4_8KhFVVzscHvOhSBWViioAyQ5wk22MzIG1QgcXd4ÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÅ