lax slack is now a flux theorem (`topBump_flux`, zero-axiom): the
contradiction bump's orbit is a single point of the germ order (every
iterate germ-equivalent to the seed) while the data never repeats and the
‚ä§-mass exceeds the iterate count ‚Äî settling holds at the order level,
fails at the data level, on one dynamic. **Strange consequence**: the
derived escape invariant cuts the regime column at the œâ-rung only,
(T,F,T,T), whereas the stipulated `cohomologyVanishes` gate cuts it
