## 8. The stochastic direction (census 2026-07-11; wing FOUNDED same day)

### 8.0 The census (pre-founding state)

A four-agent sweep of the full tree established (reading, verified against
the Lean): at census time **nothing in the library was normalized
probability.** `Calculus/Probability/Measure.lean` counts in ‚Ñï and never
divides; `MarkovKernel` rows are not constrained to sum to one;
"stationary ‚ü∫ fixed point" (`markov_stationary_is_closure_fixpoint`) is
definitional; "molecular chaos" is a rank-1 matrix fact; "sprinkling
expectation" is linearity of a finite sum. Exactly two genuine
probabilistic seeds existed: `poissonKernel` (one rational 2√ó2 chain,
decidably stationary) and `Percolation.gauge_orbit_equidistributes` ‚Äî the
uniform measure on a finite group orbit forced by transitivity, ‚ä§-rate
1/4. The second is the model: probability arriving as the measure a
symmetry *forces*. Conceptual frame (conjecture, but a good one): the
library lives at the idempotent endpoint of Maslov dequantization (¬ß1) ‚Äî
so **the stochastic program is dequantization run backward**, restoring
the multiplicity the tropical shadow forgot.

### 8.1 The founding theorems (2026-07-11)

