## 8b. The combinatorial hand (operator-dealt 2026-07-11 evening)

Five topics dealt as one hand ‚Äî chip-firing, sandpiles, o-minimal
geometry, quiver representations, Hall algebras ‚Äî and they braid: this
section records the braid and the ranked bets. Every external result
below is marked theorem-(external); nothing is claimed in-tree unless a
declaration is named. None of these names is earned (¬ß10 discipline):
Dhar, Baker‚ÄìNorine, Gabriel, Ringel enter the ledger the day their
welds are Lean, not before.

### 8b.1 Chip-firing is settling theory built by strangers

- **Stabilization is a KZ closure** (reading; the external theorem is
  Dhar's abelian property ‚Äî terminating and confluent by the diamond
  property/Newman's lemma, so "stabilize" is a well-defined idempotent
  operator on chip configurations). Natural home: the tree's `Closure`
  machinery; the abelian sandpile theorem is the statement that this
  closure exists on a finite ‚Ñ§-carrier.
- **The sandpile literature's central function is CALLED the odometer**
  (external usage, Levine‚ÄìPeres school): u(v) = firings of v during
  stabilization, characterized by the least action principle ‚Äî the
  pointwise LEAST function whose adjusted configuration is stable. A
  least-fixed-point settling certificate, sharing name and shape with
  `Closure/Odometer.lean` while being a different object ‚Äî and the
  shape (minimal witness of how much carrying it took to settle) is
  the weld to attempt.
- **The critical group is a torsion refinement of the cycle-rank
  currency** (conjecture as exchange statement; externally: critical
  group = coker of the reduced Laplacian, order = spanning-tree count
  by matrix-tree, recurrents form a torsor over it). For the PR
  context 4-cycle the rank currency says 1 while the critical group
  says ‚Ñ§/4 ‚Äî ¬ß4's exchange web prices by rank and cannot see torsion.
  Open: what obstruction quantity does the torsion price?
- **Baker‚ÄìNorine Riemann‚ÄìRoch for graphs** (theorem-external;
  formalized nowhere, to current knowledge): r(D) ‚àí r(K‚àíD) = deg(D) +
  1 ‚àí g with g = |E| ‚àí |V| + 1 ‚Äî the genus IS the cycle rank, the
  house currency. It is the divisor-graded, dualized refinement of the
  œá = »û‚Å∞ ‚àí »û¬π ledger (`AntiLandauerEntropy`). Finite, decidable,
  zero-axiom-shaped.
- Farther lights, recorded so they aren't re-derived: rotor-routing's
  free transitive action of the critical group on spanning trees (a
  second torsor); sandpile scaling limits (Pegden‚ÄìSmart,
  Levine‚ÄìPegden‚ÄìSmart ‚Äî the Apollonian structure of the identity
  element, integer superharmonic matrices) ‚Äî hard analysis, not near;
  the Ihara zeta of a graph (graph-RH ‚ü∫ Ramanujan) as a contact point
  between this hand and the trace-formula thread's Artin‚ÄìMazur red
  node.

### 8b.2 Sandpile statistics = the statistical mechanics of settling time

The regime tower classifies settling by ordinal; driven sandpiles study
the DISTRIBUTION of settling cost. Readings, each theorem-shaped at the
finite level: the drive-and-stabilize Markov chain is an evolution
whose kernel IS a settling closure ‚Äî ¬ß8.2's four verbs applied to the
settling machinery itself; its stationary law is uniform on the
recurrent torsor, FORCED by the abelian group action ‚Äî the
forced-measure doctrine of `gauge_orbit_equidistributes`, one rung up
(group orbit ‚Üí torsor); avalanche size is settling cost as a random
variable, and self-organized criticality says the stationary measure
holds the system at the boundary of its settling regimes, where that
cost is scale-free. Grain addition = a told-true tick; the recurrent
sector = the settled sector; the reading "toppling is the tally
increment under a conservation law" is unexplored and cheap to test.
Rotor-routing (the Propp machine) is the dequantized random walk ‚Äî
deterministic, with discrepancy theorems bounding its distance from
the expectation: dequantization run backward with a stated exchange
rate.

### 8b.3 O-minimality is the boundary drawn around this library

Tarski ‚Üí Wilkie ‚Üí Pila‚ÄìWilkie ‚Üí Bakker‚ÄìBrunebarbe‚ÄìTsimerman: structures
where every definable subset of the line is finitely many points and
intervals, forcing finite cell decomposition and piecewise
monotonicity in all dimensions ‚Äî Grothendieck's tame topology as model
theory. Two honest relations, no more. (1) Doctrinal: o-minimality is
the strict-finite regime imposed on geometry by axiom; the
monotonicity theorem is a regime statement. (2) Sharp: **no o-minimal
structure defines a Cantor set** ‚Äî the dyadic hull, this library's
central object, is precisely what o-minimality exists to exclude.
Where o-minimality forbids wildness, the regime tower stratifies and
prices it. Not a formalization target; a foil. Two importable
instruments: the o-minimal Euler characteristic (‚Ñ§-valued, additive,
negative-capable ‚Äî a citizen of the signed rung of ¬ß8.3's matrix,
cousin to the œá ledger), and Tarski's decidability of real-closed
fields ‚Äî semialgebraic geometry is the decidable fragment of geometry,
the fragment that already speaks the house's kernel-decidable dialect;
if real geometry is ever earned (¬ß9), that is its door. Recorded
meta-conjecture: the tame/wild dichotomy appears THREE times in this
hand (o-minimal tameness; Drozd's finite/tame/wild representation
type; sandpile regularity vs criticality) ‚Äî that these are one regime
column wearing three coats is exactly the kind of conflation this
library exists to make a theorem.

### 8b.4 Quiver representations: the exchange web's higher-rank future

Gabriel (theorem-external): finite representation type ‚ü∫ ADE,
indecomposables ‚ü∫ positive roots; Kac for the wild side; BGP
reflection functors realize the Weyl group. The direct weld: the
contextuality wing is ALREADY rank-one quiver representation theory ‚Äî
a ‚Ñ§/2-connection on the context graph is a representation of the path
groupoid, the gauge coset its iso-class, holonomy its value on cycles,
and the rank-one character variety over ùîΩ‚ÇÇ IS H¬π(G, ‚Ñ§/2), the currency
(`prConnection_flux` and ¬ß7d's unified Wilson loop are theorems about
the simplest character variety there is). Quiver theory names the
higher-rank continuation: frustration and ground states become moduli
of representations with potential ‚Äî nonabelian coins for the exchange
web. Distance is honest: Gabriel needs linear algebra the tree only
seeds (`rank_nullity_general` is the right first stone). The cheap
door: **Cartan chip-firing** ‚Äî the Mozes numbers game on Dynkin
diagrams, firing = Weyl reflection, confluence by Eriksson,
termination selecting exactly the finite root systems
(Benkart‚ÄìKlivans‚ÄìReiner for the sandpile side) ‚Äî chip-firing and
Gabriel play the same root combinatorics from opposite ends. Small
observation for later: the tower stages are representations of cyclic
quivers (affine type, tame), the Jordan quiver's nilpotent
representations are partitions, and the representation type climbing
the tower's regime column is unexplored.

### 8b.5 Hall algebras: merge-counting IS the house subject

The Ringel‚ÄìHall algebra of a finitary abelian category multiplies
iso-classes by COUNTING EXTENSIONS ‚Äî the ways two objects merge into a
third, weighted 1/|Aut|. Not an analogy: a Hall algebra's
multiplication table is a metrology of merges, and this library is a
metrology of merges in a different coefficient semiring (¬ß0). Ringel
(theorem-external): for Dynkin quivers over ùîΩ_q the merge-counting
algebra is U_q(n‚Å∫); Green's coproduct makes it a bialgebra; Lusztig's
canonical basis is its geometry. Three welds, by depth: (1) the
1/|Aut| weights are groupoid cardinality ‚Äî Boltzmann counting ‚Äî the
refined mass a record-with-symmetry should carry, needed the moment
the stochastic wing counts configurations with internal symmetry (the
sandpile torsor already asks); (2) the q ‚Üí 0 limit of quantum groups
is crystal theory ‚Äî Kashiwara crystals are the TROPICALIZATION of
U_q ‚Äî so the library, at the idempotent endpoint by proved
construction (`supp`, ¬ß1), has crystals as its native representation
theory, and the Hall algebra is the counting story `supp` shadows:
dequantization run backward through Lie theory; (3) buildable today:
Szczesny's ùîΩ‚ÇÅ-Hall algebras ‚Äî honest ‚Ñï-counting, no q ‚Äî and the Hall
structure on partitions from Jordan-quiver nilpotents (the classical
Hall algebra, Hall‚ÄìLittlewood land) is finite combinatorics in the
decidable idiom; the q-deformation waits on ¬ß9's polynomial API. Far
light, recorded not claimed: Kapranov ‚Äî the Hall algebra of coherent
sheaves on a curve over ùîΩ_q speaks automorphic forms (Eisenstein
series live in it); Burban‚ÄìSchiffmann's elliptic Hall algebra is
Macdonald/DAHA country ‚Äî the same country the RH thread's Artin‚ÄìMazur
red node squints at. The road signs agree; the road is long.

### 8b.6 Ranked bets from this hand

By the operator's criterion (frontiers of THIS territory, decidable
idiom, no new axioms):

1. **The abelian sandpile theorem as a KZ closure** ‚Äî confluence via
   the diamond property, the sandpile odometer as least settling
   certificate. Finite ‚Ñ§-linear; first-in-any-assistant candidate.
2. **Dhar's burning criterion + recurrent torsor + uniform stationary
   law** ‚Äî the stochastic wing's second forced measure, extending the
   `gauge_orbit_equidistributes` pattern from orbit to torsor.
3. **Baker‚ÄìNorine Riemann‚ÄìRoch** ‚Äî duality for the house currency;
   finite combinatorics; first-in-any-assistant candidate.
4. **The Cartan/numbers-game weld** ‚Äî chip-firing on Dynkin diagrams,
   Eriksson confluence, termination ‚ü∫ finiteness.
5. **The ùîΩ‚ÇÅ Hall monoid on partitions** ‚Äî merge-counting as an
   associative product at the dequantized point.

O-minimality deliberately absent from the bets: it is the foil, not
the target.

## 9. Infrastructure we do not have ‚Äî and how to EARN it

The census against Mathlib found four adoption-blocking absences: ‚ÑÇ,
topology, a polynomial API, Finset. Absence is a design judgment (house
law), and importing any of them would violate no-free-data anyway ‚Äî so
each must arrive in-chain or not at all. Conjectured derivations, each
with an existing trailhead in the tree:

- **‚ÑÇ from the quarter-turn.** `negSwap` has order 4 with square
  `negConf` (theorem, `D4Gauge`); the charge diamond already carries J
  with J¬≤ = ‚àí1. Conjecture: ‚ÑÇ = the Bishop-real plane with the D‚ÇÑ
  quarter-turn as multiplication by i ‚Äî earned when the J-orbit is
  welded to `RReal` pairs and the ring laws are proved. This is what
  the reading-ladder rung "trace-interval ‚Üí circle pair" and the
  Artin‚ÄìMazur spectra ("modulus 1") are waiting on. ‚ÑÇ here would not
  be posited; it would be the charge symmetry acting on the completed
  value carrier.
- **Topology from settling.** The tree already proves Alexandrov
  recovery (`causal_alexandrov_recovers_cones`: specialization order =
  causal order) and owns the profinite cylinder structure of the hull
  (`hull_separated_by_stages`, `CylinderDatum`). Conjecture: the
  library's topology is Alexandrov/Scott topology derived from its own
  orders, plus the hull's cylinder (profinite) topology ‚Äî opens as
  settling-stable predicates. General topology is not missing; it is
  latent in two proved carriers and needs stating once.
- **Polynomials from the charpoly carriers.** `StepN/Recurrence.lean`
  already has characteristic polynomials as ascending `List Int` with
  `degreeN`, `monic`, evaluation, and Cayley‚ÄìHamilton as a family
  theorem (`cayleyHamilton_vershik`). The admitted identification debt
  "no matrix the charpolys are OF" IS the missing polynomial API asking
  to exist: one owning module making list-coefficients a commutative
  ring with evaluation as a ring hom would discharge the debt and give
  Salem/Lehmer/zeta their language. The reflective `cring` normalizer
  (`RingTactic.normalize_sound`) already contains a verified normal
  form to build on.
- **Finset from the counting measure.** `SampleSpace`/`Event` (listed
  carrier + decidable indicator) is already Finset-shaped; missing is
  cardinality infrastructure (pigeonhole in general, counting under
  maps). Earning path: the counting measure IS the cardinality ‚Äî
  develop measure-algebra (image, preimage, product) and Finset arrives
  as the faithful carrier of decidable events, which the stochastic
  program (¬ß8) needs anyway. Note Ramsey is currently R(3,3) ‚â§ 6 only;
  general finite Ramsey waits on exactly this.

**The Bishop reals are the differentiated asset ‚Äî invest.** The audit
verified: `real_completeness`, `archimedean`, `mul_inv`, `sq_sqrtNat`,
`rank_nullity_general`, and the fundamental theorem of arithmetic all
carry propext/Quot.sound ONLY ‚Äî no Classical.choice anywhere ‚Äî and
rational-order facts about ‚àö5 reduce in the kernel by plain `decide`
(verified live; needs `maxRecDepth` raised). Mathlib can offer neither:
its reals are noncomputable and choice saturates everything, so its
axiom certificates are vacuous. Concrete work items: (a) the bridging
lemma lifting one decided rational inequality at one index to a `Pos`
witness on the real (a `lt_of_ratApprox_lt` shape); (b) a
normalized-rational representation so kernel `decide` scales. Those two
turn the stack into a certified-numerics tool an outsider could use.
A reflexivity worth stating plainly: treating propext and Quot.sound as
priced debt is the ‚ä§-ledger applied to the metatheory ‚Äî the library
practices its own subject on itself, and that discipline is the product.

## 10. What we have that no one else has ‚Äî and the names not yet earned

Calibrated census (checked against Mathlib, Isabelle/AFP, Coq, Agda,
Mizar to the best of current knowledge). **Likely first in any proof
assistant, already machine-checked here:**

1. **Causal set theory** ‚Äî the general Benincasa‚ÄìDowker d'Alembertian,
   M√∂bius inversion on the causal poset (`mobius_orthogonality`), the
   Ricci-scalar/BD-action identity
   (`total_ricciScalar_eq_two_bdAction`), Alexandrov recovery. No proof
   assistant has any causal set theory. The strongest claim we own; the
   continuum limit and genuine sprinkling remain the honest frontier.
2. **The constructive Tsirelson tier** 2 < 2‚àö2 < 4 on Bishop reals
   (`chsh_tsirelson_tier`), and KCBS at ‚àö5 ‚Äî analytic quantum bounds
   with meaningful axiom certificates.
3. **The dyadic odometer** with axiom-free successor, Cantor-hull
   inverse limit, and proved minimal-aperiodic dynamics ‚Äî Mathlib has
   ergodic theory but no Bratteli‚ÄìVershik/odometer systems.
4. **The unified Wilson loop** (¬ß7d) ‚Äî curvature and contextuality as
   two projections of one gauge charge, which no formalism anywhere
   has as a theorem.
5. **Formalization under inconsistency** (capability, not one theorem
   ‚Äî reading, with its theorem components green). In every other proof
   assistant an inconsistent premise set proves everything, so a
   contradictory theory/dataset/specification cannot be formalized at
   all, only avoided. Here inconsistency is a value with a price (held
   ‚ä§; `topMass`, »û¬π as its exact cost), so a contradictory object can
   be admitted as an object of study and machine-checked theorems
   proved about what its contradiction costs and where it lives. The
   blueprint already carries the computational form: gates as local
   transport rules on the held ‚ä§-mirror, computing paraconsistently
   from the contradiction without explosion (the charge-holonomy
   automaton read as a paraconsistent circuit). State this as a
   capability of the value layer, never as a single citation.

Adjacent verbatim finding (Collatz session, transcript-confirmed):
**linear forms in logarithms have never been formalized in any proof
assistant** ‚Äî Baker/Rhin territory, and the parent-barrier gap's Pad√©
log‚ÇÇ3 measure is this territory's constructive doorstep. Not claimed;
recorded as the measured distance of that frontier.

**The unearned names (a ledger, not shame ‚Äî each entry states its
price).** We rename nothing; we earn or we strike. Current debts, with
earning paths: *Landauer's principle* is presently an alias of cycle
rank ‚Äî earned when kT¬∑ln 2 is a real quantity (ln 2 via `logNat`
exists; the missing weld is an entropy inequality on an actual process,
which ¬ß8's measures make possible). *CALM* ‚Äî the file itself says the
biconditional is not witnessed; earned by proving monotone ‚ü∫
coordination-free over a real consistency model, not the lattice
conjunction. *Jeandel‚ÄìRao* is a cohomology marker, not the 11-tile
set; earned only by the tile set and its aperiodicity (and Wang-tiling
undecidability already exists in Coq/Isabelle ‚Äî even earned, not a
first). *Lehmer* is a Bool shadow (the FOUR-valued reclassification in
the RH thread is the honest repair). *Ornstein‚ÄìZernike, Debye,
Boltzmann-H* are lattice least-fixed-points with the analytics absent;
each is earned only past a Fourier/exponential layer that does not
exist yet. *CRN deficiency theory* is absent entirely ‚Äî only detailed
balance and a Petri-net Lyapunov descent exist. Until earned, these
names cite their blueprint red nodes, never the certificates (¬ß the
reading-ledger discipline).

## 11. The near horizon (NOT the remembered thing ‚Äî see caution)

Things no one has formalized anywhere that the existing carriers put
within a few sessions' reach, ranked by novelty √ó proximity:

1. **The genuine Abramsky‚ÄìMansfield‚ÄìBarbosa ƒåech obstruction** ‚Äî the
   actual cohomology of the presheaf of local sections, with H¬π ‚â† 0 ‚ü∫
   strong contextuality on PR/KCBS. Never machine-verified anywhere;
   our current version is the Boolean parity stand-in; the presheaf
   carriers (`Model`, `CompatibleFamily`, the nerve) already exist.
2. **Fine's theorem for the PR box** (`EmpiricalModel.lean` names it
   itself as the natural next step).
3. **Uniqueness of the 4D Benincasa‚ÄìDowker coefficients** (1,‚àí9,16,‚àí8)
   from the moment system ‚Äî pure linear algebra, 2D uniqueness already
   proved (`bdCoeff2_unique`).
4. **Unique ergodicity of the odometer** ‚Äî where this section and ¬ß8
   are the same theorem.
