  (`Language/Settling.lean` + `Cohomology/N.lean`) and could mint the
  first machine-checked taxonomy of semantic paradox by dimension.

### (e) GHZ = Borromean = Massey: one knot

The received name for "pairwise trivial, globally obstructed" is the
**Massey product**: when pairwise cup products vanish, a triple
product lives one degree higher ‚Äî the precise algebra of ¬ß12i's
arbitration reading. Its mascot is the **Borromean rings**: three
loops, pairwise unlinked, globally inseparable ‚Äî the classical
nonzero Massey product. And the quantum literature already knows
(Aravind's observation, reading) that the **GHZ state is Borromean**:
trace out any one particle and the remaining pair is unentangled;
the tripartite whole is maximally entangled. Chain complete:

  GHZ (the tree's ranked hypergraph item, ¬ß4/¬ß6) = Borromean linkage
  = nonzero Massey product = the first degree-2 arbitration class,
  priced in ‚ä§.

The all-versus-nothing GHZ argument is not a bigger PR box; it is a
different SPECIES of obstruction ‚Äî one that pairwise invariants
(cycle rank, the ¬ß4 currencies) provably cannot see, because its
pairwise shadows all vanish. When the hypergraph-ùîΩ‚ÇÇ program lands,
state its headline theorem in this form: the GHZ ‚ä§-ground-state is
nonzero while every pairwise restriction's ground state is zero ‚Äî
the tree's first Massey-type invariant, and (reading) the first
machine-checked one anywhere in any coefficient system.

### (f) The knitting obstruction is an H¬≤ class

The weave (`WeaveDraft`: bilattice-coloured sofic shift, miscrossing
